    ":question/math-academy-id": "e-15606",
    ":question/problem": "Suppose $|\\,\\mathbf{a}\\,|=13$ and the angle between vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ is $\\theta = \\dfrac{2\\pi}{3}.$ Find the scalar projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}.$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =|\\,a\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =13\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =13\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{13}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  },
