      ":question/problem": "Suppose $|\\,t\\,|=\\sqrt{2}$ and the angle between vectors $t$ and $u$ is $\\theta =\\frac{3\\pi }{4}.$ Find the scalar projection of $t$ onto $u.$\n\n${\\text{comp}}_{u}\\,t=$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{u}\\,t & =|\\,t\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}cos\\,(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
